2. Rolling-Unet implementation portions

Source: Rolling-Unet, https://github.com/Jiaoyang45/Rolling-Unet
Revision: 8a43d40c218917e454c0584a853757e3a2cf9c80
The adapted implementation portions are:
- asni_net/layers.py: ConvStage and TokenProjection.
- asni_net/model.py: the retained encoder/decoder layer configuration and
  surrounding data flow (pooling, normalization, additive skip connections,
  upsampling and output projection).
- asni_net/initialization.py: layer-initialization rules and the construction
  sequence retained to reproduce the frozen experiment's starting parameters.

The SIP weighted fusion, NI computation and their integration with channel
mapping are project-specific changes. The original rolling token mixer and
DSC forward branch are not used. This notice identifies implementation
provenance; it does not attribute the general encoder-decoder concept or the
ASNI-Net method as a whole to Rolling-Unet. The axial sampling design reference
is listed separately in section 3.

